# WeatherBoard — variable names only. Copy to .env for local worker development.
# .env is git-ignored. NEVER put a real value in this file or in any file that is
# committed, and never inline a key into chat, a commit message or a screenshot.

# --- Server-side only (edge API proxy: worker/) -----------------------------
# OpenWeatherMap — primary weather provider (Free "Weather API": current +
# 5-day/3-hour forecast). New keys can take up to ~2 hours to activate.
OWM_API_KEY=

# GeoDB Cities via RapidAPI — city autocomplete.
# Basic plan: 1,000 requests/day, 1 request/second, at most 10 results per page.
RAPIDAPI_KEY=

# --- Background push: NOT IMPLEMENTED --------------------------------------
# No VAPID or push variables are read by this project. A genuine closed-browser
# reminder needs a deployed sender, a durable subscription store, a scheduler and
# VAPID keys; this environment has none of them. See README → Push reminders (C8).
# Adding the names here would imply a feature that does not exist.

# --- Client-side -----------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately empty: the browser bundle needs no credentials. Anything
# prefixed VITE_ is compiled into public JS, so keys must never use that prefix.
